hadiths[219]{hadithnumber,text}:
"5540","It was narrated from 'Umar that:When the prohibition of Khamr was revealed, 'Umar said: ""O Allah, give us a clear ruling on Khamr,"" and the Verse in Al-Baqarah was revealed. 'Umar was called and it was recited to him. Then 'Umar said: ""O Allah, give us a clear ruling on Khamr,"" and the Verse in An-Nisa' was revealed: ""O you who believe! Approach not As-Salah (the prayer) when you are in a drunken state"". And when the Iqamah for prayer was said, the caller of the Messenger of Allah [SAW] would cry out: ""O you who believe! Approach not As-Salah (the prayer) when you are in a drunken state."" 'Umar was called and this was recited to him. Then he said: ""O Allah, give us a clear ruling on Khamr."" Then the Verse in Surat Al-Ma'idah was revealed, and 'Umar was called, and it was recited to him. When he reached the words, ""So, will you not then abstain?,"" 'Umar said: ""We have abstained, we have abstained"
"5541","It was narrated that Anas bin Malik said:\\""When Khamr was forbidden"""""
"5542","It was narrated that Jabir - meaning bin 'Abdullah - said:\\""Unripe dates and dried dates are Khamr"""""
"5543","Jabir bin 'Abdullah said:\\""Unripe dates and dried dates are Khamr.\""\"" Al-A'mash narrated it in Marfu' form"""""
"5544","It was narrated from Jabir that:The Prophet [SAW] said: \\""Raisins and dried dates are Khamr"""""
"5545","Jabir bin 'Abdullah said:\Unripe dates and dried dates are Khamr.\"" Al-A'mash narrated it in Marfu' form."""""
"5546","It was narrated that Ibn 'Abbas said:\\""The Messenger of Allah [SAW] forbade Ad-Dubba'"""""
"5547","It was narrated that Ibn 'Abbas said:\\""The Messenger of Allah [SAW] forbade Ad-Dubba'"""""
"5548","It was narrated that Abu Sa'eed Al-Khudri said:\\""The Messenger of Allah [SAW] forbade (mixing) Az-Zahuw and At-Tamr"""""
"5549","Abdullah bin Abi Qatadah narrated from his father that:The Prophet [SAW] said: \\""Do not combine dried dates with raisins"""""
"5550","It was narrated from Abu Qatadah that:The Messenger of Allah [SAW] said: \\""Do not soak Az-Zahuw and ripe dates together"""""
"5551","It was narrated that Abu Sa'eed Al-Khudri said:\\""The Messenger of Allah [SAW] forbade mixing dried dates and raisins"""""
"5552","Ata' narrated from Jabir that:The Prophet [SAW] forbade mixing dried dates and raisins"
"5553","It was narrated that Abu Sa'eed Al-Khudri said:\The Messenger of Allah [SAW] forbade mixing dried dates and raisins"
"5554","It was narrated from Jabir that:The Messenger of Allah [SAW] forbade soaking raisins and dried dates together"
"5555","It was narrated that Ibn 'Abbas said:\\""The Messenger of Allah [SAW] forbade Ad-Dubba'"""""
"5556","It was narrated that Ibn 'Abbas said:\\""Al-Busr on their own are unlawful and with dried dates they are unlawful"""""
"5557","It was narrated that Ibn 'Abbas said:\\""The Messenger of Allah [SAW] forbade mixing dried dates and raisins"""""
"5558","Jabir bin 'Abdullah said:\\""The Messenger of Allah [SAW] forbade dried dates and raisins"""""
"5559","It was narrated that Ibn 'Abbas said:\The Messenger of Allah [SAW] forbade mixing dried dates and raisins"
"5560","It was narrated from Jabir that :The Messenger of Allah [SAW] forbade soaking raisins and Al-Busr together"
"5561","It was narrated that Anas bin Malik said:\\""The Messenger of Allah [SAW] forbade us to soak two things together when one is more potent than the other. I asked him about Fadikh (a drink made from fresh dates cut open) and he forbade it. He disliked the extra bit on Al-Busr"""""
"5562","It was narrated that Abu Idris said:\\""I saw Anas bin Malik when some Busr which had extra bits were brought to him"""""
"5563","It was narrated that :Anas would not leave any dates that had become ripe but he would remove them from his Fadikh"
"5564","It was narrated from Abu Qatadah that:The Messenger of Allah [SAW] said: \\""Do not soak Az-Zahuw and ripe dates together"""""
"5565","It was narrated that Abu Sa'eed Al-Khudri said:\\""The Messenger of Allah [SAW] forbade mixing Al-Busr with dried dates"""""
"5566","Abu Sa'eed Al-Khudri narrated that:The Prophet [SAW] forbade mixing Al-Busr with dried dates"
"5567","Abu Hurairah said:\\""The Messenger of Allah [SAW] forbade mixing Al-Busr and raisins"""""
"5568","It was narrated from Abu Sa'eed Al-Khudri that:The Prophet [SAW] forbade soaking dried dates and raisins"
"5569","Abu Hurairah said:\\""The Messenger of Allah [SAW] said: 'Khamr comes from these two.'\""\"" Suwaid (one of the narrators) said: \""\""From these two trees: The date palm and the grapevine"""""
"5570","It was narrated that Abu Hurairah said:\\""The Messenger of Allah [SAW] said: 'Khamr comes from these two trees: The date palm and the grapevine"""""
"5571","It was narrated from Al-Mughirah that Ibrahim and Al-Sha'bi said:\\""Strong drink is Khamr"""""
"5572","It was narrated that Sa'eed bin Jubair said:\\""Strong drink is Khamr"""""
"5573","It was narrated that Sa'eed bin Jubair said:\\""Strong drink is Khamr"""""
"5574","It was narrated that Sa'eed bin Jubair said:\\""Strong drink is unlawful"""""
"5575","It was narrated that Sa'eed bin Jubair said:\Strong drink is Khamr.\"""""""
"5576","It was narrated that Ibn 'Umar said:\\""I heard 'Umar bin Al-Khattab"""""
"5577","It was narrated that Ibn 'Umar said:\\""Khamr is made from five things: From dates"""""
"5578","It was narrated that Ibn Sirin said:\\""A man came to Ibn 'Umar and said: 'Our families make drinks for us by soaking (fruits) at night"""""
"5579","It was narrated from Ibn 'Umar that:The Prophet [SAW] said: \\""Every intoxicant is unlawful and every intoxicant is Khamr"""""
"5580","It was narrated that Ibn 'Umar said:\\""The Messenger of Allah [SAW] said: 'Every intoxicant is unlawful and every intoxicant is Khamr"""""
"5581","It was narrated that Ibn 'Umar said:\\""The Messenger of Allah [SAW] said: 'Every intoxicant is Khamr"""""
"5582","It was narrated that Ibn 'Umar said:\\""The Messenger of Allah [SAW] said: 'Every intoxicant is Khamr and every intoxicant is unlawful"""""
"5583","It was narrated from Ibn 'Umar that:The Prophet [SAW] said: \\""Every intoxicant is unlawful and every intoxicant is Khamr"""""
"5584","It was narrated from Ibn 'Umar that:The Prophet [SAW] said: \\""Every intoxicant is unlawful"""""
"5585","It was narrated that Abu Hurairah said:\\""The Messenger of Allah [SAW] said: 'Every intoxicant is unlawful"""""
"5586","It was narrated from Abu Hurairah that:The Messenger of Allah [SAW] forbade soaking (fruits) in Ad-Dubba'"
"5587","It was narrated from 'Aishah that:The Prophet [SAW] said: \\""Do not soak (fruits) in Ad-Dubba'"""""
"5588","It was narrated that 'Aishah said:\\""The Messenger of Allah [SAW] said: 'Every drink that intoxicates is unlawful.'\""\"" Qutaibah (one of the narrators) said: \""\""From the Prophet [SAW]"""""
"5589","It was narrated from Abu Hurairah that:The Messenger of Allah [SAW] forbade soaking (fruits) in Ad-Dubba', Al-Muzaffat, An-Naqir, Al-Hantam, and every intoxicant is unlawful."
"5590","It was narrated from 'Aishah that:The Prophet [SAW] said: \Do not soak (fruits) in Ad-Dubba'"
"5591","It was narrated from 'Aishah that:The Prophet [SAW] was asked about mead and he said: \\""Every drink that intoxicates is unlawful.\""\"" And mead is a drink made of honey"""""
"5592","It was narrated that Abu Musa said:\\""The Messenger of Allah [SAW] said: 'Every intoxicant is unlawful"""""
"5593","It was narrated from Abu Burdah that his father said:\\""The Messenger of Allah [SAW] sent Mu'adh and me to Yemen. Mu'adh said: 'You are sending us to a land where the people have many kinds of drinks. What should I drink?' He said: 'Drink"""""
"5594","It was narrated that Abu Musa said:\\""The Messenger of Allah [SAW] said: 'Every intoxicant is unlawful"""""
"5595","Al-Aswad bin Shaiban As-Sadusi said:\\""I heard 'Ata' being asked by a man: 'We travel and drinks are offered to us in the marketplaces"""""
"5596","It was narrated that Ibn Sirin said:\\""Every intoxicant is unlawful"""""
"5597","It was narrated that 'Abdul-Malik bin At-Tufail Al-Jazari said:\\""Umar bin 'Abdul-Aziz wrote to us"""""
"5598","It was narrated that As-Sa'q bin Hazn said:\\""Umar bin 'Abdul-'Aziz wrote to 'Adiy bin Artah (saying): 'Every intoxicant is unlawful"""""
"5599","It was narrated from Abu Musa Al-Ash'ari that:The Messenger of Allah [SAW] said: \\""Every intoxicant is unlawful"""""
"5600","Abu Bakr bin Abi Musa narrated that his father said:\\""The Messenger of Allah [SAW] sent me to Yemen and I said: 'O Messenger of Allah"""""
"5601","It was narrated from Abu Burdah that his father said:\\""The Messenger of Allah [SAW] sent me to Yemen and I said: 'O Messenger of Allah"""""
"5602","It was narrated that Ibn 'Umar said:\\""The Messenger of Allah [SAW] delivered a Khutbah and quoted the Verse about Khamr. A man said: 'O Messenger of Allah"""""
"5603","It was narrated that Abu Al-Juwairiyah said:\\""I heard Ibn 'Abbas when he was asked: 'Advise us about Badhiq (a drink made from the juice of grapes slightly boiled).' He said: 'Muhammad came before Badhiq (i.e."""""
"5604","It was narrated from Abu Burdah that his father said:\The Messenger of Allah [SAW] sent me to Yemen and I said: 'O Messenger of Allah"
"5605","It was narrated that Ibn 'Umar said:\The Messenger of Allah [SAW] delivered a Khutbah and quoted the Verse about Khamr. A man said: 'O Messenger of Allah"
"5606","It was narrated that Abu Al-Juwairiyah said:\I heard Ibn 'Abbas when he was asked: 'Advise us about Badhiq (a drink made from the juice of grapes slightly boiled).' He said: 'Muhammad came before Badhiq (i.e."
"5607","It was narrated that Abu Hurairah said:\\""I know that the Messenger of Allah [SAW] was fasting"""""
"5608","It was narrated that 'Ali - may Allah honor his face - said:\\""The Prophet [SAW] forbade to me to use gold rings"""""
"5609","Sa'sa'ah said to 'Ali bin Abi Talib - may Allah honor his face - :\\""Forbid to us"""""
"5610","It was narrated from Jabir that :(fruits) would be soaked for the Prophet [SAW] in a small vessel made of stone"
"5611","It was narrated that Tawus said:\\""A man said to Ibn 'Umar: 'Did the Messenger of Allah [SAW] forbid soaking (fruits) in earthenware jars?' He said: 'Yes.' Tawus said: 'By Allah"""""
"5612","It was narrated that Sulaiman At-Taimi and Ibrahim bin Maisarah said:\\""We heard Tawus say: 'A man came to Ibn 'Umar and said: Did the Messenger of Allah [SAW] forbid soaking (fruits) in earthenware jars? He said: 'Yes.' Ibrahim added in his Hadith: \""\""And Ad-Dubba' (gourds)"""""
"5613","Ibn 'Abbas said:\\""The Messenger of Allah [SAW] forbade soaking (fruits) in earthenware jars"""""
"5614","It was narrated that Ibn 'Umar said:\\""The Messenger of Allah [SAW] forbade Al-Hantam. I (the narrator) said: \""\""What is Al-Hantam?\""\"" He said: \""\""The earthenware jar"""""
"5615","It was narrated that Abu Maslamah said:\\""I heard 'Abdul-'Aziz - that is"""""
"5616","It was narrated that Sa'eed bin Jubair said:\\""We asked Ibn 'Umar about Nabidh made in an earthenware jar and he said: 'The Messenger of Allah [SAW] forbade that.' So I went to Ibn 'Abbas and said to him: 'Today I heard something that surprised me.' He said: 'What was it?' I said: 'I asked Ibn 'Umar about Nabidh made in an earthenware jar and he said: The Messenger of Allah [SAW] forbade it.' He said: 'Ibn 'Umar spoke the truth.' I said: 'What is an earthenware jar?' He said: 'Anything that is made of clay"""""
"5617","It was narrated that Sa'eed bin Jubair said:\\""I was with Ibn 'Umar when he was asked about Nabidh made in an earthenware jar. He said: 'The Messenger of Allah [SAW] forbade it.' I got upset when I heard that"""""
"5618","It was narrated that Ash-Shaibani said:\\""I heard Ibn Abi Awfa say: 'The Messenger of Allah [SAW] forbade Nabidh made in green earthenware jars.' I said: 'And white ones?' He said: 'I do not know"""""
"5619","Abu Ishaq Ash-Shaibani said:\\""I heard Ibn Abi Awfa say: 'The Messenger of Allah [SAW] forbade Nabidh made in green and white earthenware jars"""""
"5620","It was narrated that Abu Raja' said:\\""I asked Al-Hasan about Nabidh made in earthenware jars - is it unlawful? He said: '(It is) unlawful. One who would not lie narrated to us that the Messenger of Allah [SAW] forbade Nabidh made in Al-Hantam"""""
"5621","It was narrated from Ibn 'Umar that:The Messenger of Allah [SAW] forbade Ad-Dubba' (gourds)"
"5622","It was narrated from Ibn 'Umar that:The Messenger of Allah [SAW] forbade Ad-Dubba' (gourds)"
"5623","It was narrated that 'Aishah said:\\""The Messenger of Allah [SAW] forbade Ad-Dubba' (gourds) and Al-Muzaffat"""""
"5624","It was narrated from 'Ali - may Allah honor his face - that:The Prophet [SAW] forbade Ad-Dubba' (gourds) and Al-Muzaffat"
"5625","It was narrated from 'Abdur-Rahman bin Ya'mar that:The Prophet [SAW] forbade Ad-Dubba' and Al-Muzaffat"
"5626","It was narrated from Anas bin Malik that:The Messenger of Allah [SAW] forbade soaking (fruits) in Ad-Dubba' (gourds) and Al-Muzaffat"
"5627","Abu Hurairah said:\\""The Messenger of Allah [SAW] forbade soaking (fruits) in Ad-Dubba' (gourds) and Al-Muzaffat"""""
"5628","It was narrated from Ibn 'Umar that :The Messenger of Allah [SAW] forbade Al-Muzaffat and squashes"
"5629","It was narrated from Ibn 'Umar that :The Messenger of Allah [SAW] forbade Ad-Dubba' (gourds)"
"5630","It was narrated that Abu Sa'eed Al-Khudri said:The Messenger of Allah [SAW] forbade drinking from green pitchers"
"5631","Ibn 'Umar said:\\""The Messenger of Allah [SAW] forbade Ad-Dubba' (gourds)"""""
"5632","Abu Hurairah said:\\""The Messenger of Allah [SAW] forbade earthenware jars"""""
"5633","Aishah said:\\""I heard the Messenger of Allah [SAW] forbidding drinks made in Dubba' (gourds)"""""
"5634","Abu Hurairah said:\\""The Messenger of Allah [SAW] forbade Ad-Dubba' (gourds)"""""
"5635","Thumamah bin Hazn Al-Qushairi said:\\""I met 'Aishah and asked her about Nabidh. She said: 'The delegation of 'Abdul-Qais came to the Messenger of Allah [SAW] and asked him in which vessels they should soak (fruits - to make Nabidh). The Prophet [SAW] forbade them to soak (fruits) in Ad-Dubba' (gourds)"""""
"5636","'Aishah said:\I heard the Messenger of Allah [SAW] forbidding drinks made in Dubba' (gourds)"
"5637","It was narrated from Ishaq - he is Ibn Suwaid - that he said:\\""Mu'adhah narrated to me from 'Aishah"""""
"5638","It was narrated that Hunaidah bint Sharik bin Aban said:\\""I met 'Aishah"""""
"5639","It was narrated that Anas said:\\""The Messenger of Allah [SAW] forbade Al-Muzaffat"""""
"5640","Sa'eed bin Jubair narrated that:He heard Ibn 'Umar and Ibn 'Abbas testify that the Messenger of Allah [SAW] forbade Ad-Dubba' (gourds)"
"5641","It was narrated from Asma' bint Yazid that:A paternal uncle of hers whose name was Anas said: \\""Ibn 'Abbas said: Does not Allah say: \""\""And whatsoever the Messenger (Muhammad) gives you"""""
"5642","Zadan said:\\""I asked 'Abdullah bin 'Umar: 'Tell me of something that you heard from the Messenger of Allah [SAW] concerning vessels and explain it.' He said: 'The Messenger of Allah [SAW] forbade Al-Hantam"""""
"5643","It was narrated that Abu Hurairah said:\\""The Messenger of Allah [SAW] forbade the delegation of 'Abdul-Qais"""""
"5644","It was narrated from Asma' bint Yazid that:A paternal uncle of hers whose name was Anas said: ""Ibn 'Abbas said: Does not Allah say: ""And whatsoever the Messenger (Muhammad) gives you, take it; and whatsoever he forbids you, abstain (from it).'? He said: 'Yes.' He said: 'Does not Allah say: 'It is not for a believer, man or woman, when Allah and His Messenger have decreed a matter that they should have any option in their decision?' I said: 'Yes.' He said: 'I bear witness that the Prophet of Allah [SAW] forbade An-Naqir, Al-Muqayyar, Ad-Dubba', and Al-Hantam"
"5645","It was narrated that Jabir said:\\""(Fruit) would be soaked for the Messenger of Allah [SAW] in a water skin"""""
"5646","It was narrated from Jabir that:The Messenger of Allah [SAW] forbade Ad-Dubba' (gourds)"
"5647","It was narrated from 'Abdullah that:The Prophet [SAW] granted a concession allowing earthenware jars that are not coated with pitch"
"5648","It was narrated from Ibn Buraidah that his father said:\\""The Messenger of Allah [SAW] said: 'I used to forbid you (to store) the sacrificial meat"""""
"5649","It was narrated from 'Abdullah bin Buraidah that his father said:\\""The Messenger of Allah [SAW] said: 'I used to forbid you to visit graves"""""
"5650","It was narrated from Ibn Buraidah that his father said:\\""The Messenger of Allah [SAW] said: 'I used to forbid three things to you: Visiting graves"""""
"5651","It was narrated from 'Abdullah bin Buraidah that his father said:\\""The Messenger of Allah [SAW] said: 'I used to forbid certain kinds of vessels to you. Now soak (fruits) in whatever you wish"""""
"5652","Abdullah bin Buraidah (narrated) from his father that:While the Messenger of Allah [SAW] was walking"
"5653","It was narrated from Jabir that :When the Messenger of Allah [SAW] forbade large water skins that are cut from the top and can no longer be closed"
"5654","It was narrated that Abu Hurairah said:\\""On the night on which he was taken on the Night Journey (Al-Isra')"""""
"5655","Ibn Muhairiz narrated from a man among the Companions of the Prophet [SAW] that :The Prophet [SAW] said: \\""People among my Ummah will drink Khamr"""""
"5656","It was narrated that Abu Hurairah said:\\""The Messenger of Allah [SAW] said: 'The adulterer is not a believer at the moment when he is committing adultery"""""
"5657","It was narrated from Abu Hurairah that:The Prophet [SAW] said: \\""The adulterer is not a believer at the moment when he is committing adultery"""""
"5658","It was narrated that Ibn 'Umar and a number of the Companions of Muhammad [SAW] said:\\""The Messenger of Allah [SAW] said: 'Whoever drinks Khamr"""""
"5659","It was narrated from Abu Hurairah that :The Messenger of Allah [SAW] said: \\""If he becomes drunk"""""
"5660","It was narrated from Abu Hurairah that:The Prophet [SAW] said: \The adulterer is not a believer at the moment when he is committing adultery"
"5661","Urwah bin Ruwaim narrated that :Ibn Ad-Dailami rode looking for 'Abdullah bin 'Amr bin Al-'As. Ibn Ad-Dailami said: \\""I entered upon him and said: 'O 'Abdullah bin 'Amr"""""
"5662","It was narrated that Masruq said:\\""If a judge accepts a gift he has consumed something unlawful"""""
"5663","It was narrated from Abu Bakr bin 'Abdur-Rahman bin Al-Harith that his father said:\\""I heard 'Uthman"""""
"5664","Abu Bakr bin 'Abdur-Rahman bin Al-Harith narrated that his father said:\\""I heard 'Uthman say: 'Avoid Khamr for it is the mother of all evils. There was a man among those who came before you who was a devoted worshipper and used to stay away from people.'\""\"" And he mentioned something similar. He said: \""\""Avoid Khamr for"""""
"5665","It was narrated that Ibn 'Umar said:\\""Whoever drinks Khamr and does not get intoxicated"""""
"5666","It was narrated from 'Abdullah bin 'Amr that:The Prophet [SAW] said: \\""Whoever drinks Khamr and puts it in his belly"""""
"5667","It was narrated that 'Abdullah bin Ad-Dailami said:\\""I entered upon 'Abdullah bin 'Amr bin Al-'As when he was in a garden of his in At-Ta'if called Al-Waht. He was walking and holding hands with a young man of Quraish who was suspected of drinking Khamr. He said: 'I heard the Messenger of Allah [SAW] say: Whoever drinks Khamr once"""""
"5668","It was narrated from Ibn 'Umar that:The Messenger of Allah [SAW] said: \\""Whoever drinks Khamr in this world and does not repent from that"""""
"5669","It was narrated from 'Abdullah bin 'Amr that:The Prophet [SAW] said: \\""No one who reminds others of his favors"""""
"5670","It was narrated from Ibn 'Umar that :The Prophet [SAW] said: \\""Whoever drinks Khamr in this world and dies addicted to it"""""
"5671","It was narrated that Ibn 'Umar said:\\""The Messenger of Allah [SAW] said: 'Whoever drinks Khamr in this world and dies addicted to it"""""
"5672","It was narrated that Ad-Dahhak said:\\""Whoever dies addicted to Khamr will have boiling water thrown in his face when he departs this world"""""
"5673","It was narrated from Ibn 'Umar that :The Prophet [SAW] said: \Whoever drinks Khamr in this world and dies addicted to it"
"5674","It was narrated that Abu Burdah bin Niyar said:\\""The Messenger of Allah [SAW] said: 'Drink from vessels but do not become intoxicated"""""
"5675","It was narrated that Ad-Dahhak said:\Whoever dies addicted to Khamr will have boiling water thrown in his face when he departs this world.\"""""""
"5676","It was narrated that Sa'eed bin Al-Musayyab said:\'Umar"
"5677","It was narrated from Qudamah Al-'Amiri that Jasrah bint Dijajah Al-'Amiriyyah told him:\\""I heard 'Aishah when some people asked her about Nabidh"""""
"5678","It was narrated that 'Ali bin Al-Mubarak said:\\""Karimah bint Hammam told me that she heard 'Aishah"""""
"5679","It was narrated that 'Aishah was asked about drinks and she said:\\""The Messenger of Allah [SAW] used to forbid all intoxicants.\""\"" And they use the narration of 'Abdullah bin Shaddad from 'Abdullah bin 'Abbas"""""
"5680","It was narrated from Ibn Shubrumah who mentioned it from 'Abdullah bin Shaddad bin Al-Had"
"5681","It was narrated that Ibn 'Abbas said:\\""Khamr was forbidden in and of itself in small or large amounts"""""
"5682","It was narrated that Ibn 'Abbas said:\\""Khamr was forbidden in and of itself"""""
"5683","It was narrated that Ibn 'Abbas said:\\""Khamr was forbidden in small or large amounts"""""
"5684","It was narrated that Abu Al-Juwairiyah Al-Jarmi said:\\""I asked Ibn 'Abbas"""""
"5685","Ibn 'Abbas said:\\""Whoever would like to regard as forbidden that which Allah and His Messenger [SAW] regard as forbidden"""""
"5686","It was narrated from 'Uyainah bin 'Abdur-Rahman that his father said:\\""A man said to Ibn 'Abbas: 'I am a man from Khurasan"""""
"5687","It was narrated that Ibn 'Abbas said:\\""Nabidh made from Al-Busr is forbidden and is not permissible"""""
"5688","It was narrated that Abu Hamzah said:\\""I used to interpret between Ibn 'Abbas and the people. A woman came to him and asked him about Nabidh made in earthenware jars"""""
"5689","Abu Hamzah Nasr said:\\""I said to Ibn 'Abbas that my grandmother makes Nabidh in an earthenware jar and it is sweet. If I drink a lot of it and sit with people"""""
"5690","It was narrated that Qais bin Wahban said:\\""I asked Ibn 'Abbas: 'I have a small jar in which I make Nabidh and when it has bubbled and settled down again"""""
"5691","It was narrated that Abu Hamzah said:\I used to interpret between Ibn 'Abbas and the people. A woman came to him and asked him about Nabidh made in earthenware jars"
"5692","Narrated from 'Abdul-Malik bin Nafi' from Ibn 'Umar:A similar report was narrated from 'Abdul-Malik bin Nafi' from Ibn 'Umar"
"5693","It was narrated from Ibn 'Umar that:A man asked about drinks and he said: \\""Avoid everything that intoxicates"""""
"5694","It was narrated that Zaid bin Jubair said:\\""I asked Ibn 'Umar about drinks and he said: 'Avoid everything that intoxicates"""""
"5695","It was narrated that Ibn 'Umar said:\\""Intoxicants are unlawful in small or large amounts"""""
"5696","It was narrated that Ibn 'Umar said:\\""Every intoxicant is Khamr and every intoxicant is unlawful"""""
"5697","It was narrated that Zaid bin Jubair said:\I asked Ibn 'Umar about drinks and he said: 'Avoid everything that intoxicates.'\"""""""
"5698","It was narrated that Ibn 'Umar said:\\""The Messenger of Allah [SAW] said: 'Every intoxicant is unlawful and every intoxicant is Khamr"""""
"5699","Ruqaiyah bint 'Amr bin Sa'd said:\\""I was under the care of Ibn 'Umar"""""
"5700","It was narrated that Abu Mas'ud said:\\""The Prophet [SAW] became thirsty around the Ka'bah so he called for a drink. Some Nabidh was brought in a water skin and he smelled it and frowned. He said: 'Bring me a bucket of Zamzam (water).' He poured it over it and drank some. A man said: 'Is it unlawful"""""
"5701","Abu Hurairah said:\\""I knew that the Messenger of Allah [SAW] was fasting on certain days"""""
"5702","Ruqaiyah bint 'Amr bin Sa'd said:\I was under the care of Ibn 'Umar"
"5703","It was narrated from Yahya bin Sa'eed who heard Sa'eed bin Al-Musayyab say:\\""Thaqif welcomed 'Umar with a drink. He called for it"""""
"5704","It was narrated that 'Utbah bin Farqad said:\\""The Nabidh that 'Umar bin Al-Khattab used to drink had turned to vinegar"""""
"5705","It was narrated from As-Sa'ib that :'Umar bin Al-Khattab went out t them and said: \\""I noticed the smell of drink on so-and-so"""""
"5706","It was narrated from Jabir that:A man from (the tribe of) Jaishan"
"5707","It was narrated that An-Nu'man bin Bashir said:\\""I heard the Messenger of Allah [SAW] say: 'That which is lawful is clear and that which is unlawful is clear"""""
"5708","It was narrated that Abu Al-Hawra' As-Sa'di said:\\""I said to Al-Hasan bin 'Ali"""""
"5709","It was narrated from Jabir that:A man from (the tribe of) Jaishan, who are from Yemen, came and asked the Messenger of Allah [SAW] about a drink that they drank in his homeland that was made of corn and called Al-Mizr (beer). The Prophet [SAW] said to him: ""Is it an intoxicant?"" He said: ""Yes."" The Messenger of Allah [SAW] said: ""Every intoxicant is unlawful. Allah, the Mighty and Sublime, has promised the one who drinks intoxicants that He will give him to drink from the mud of Khibal."" They said: ""O Messenger of Allah, what is the mud of Khibal?"" He said: ""The sweat of the people of Hell,"" or he said: ""The juice of the people of Hell"
"5710","It was narrated that Mus'ab bin Sa'd said:\\""Sa'd had many grapevines and he had someone looking after them for him. (The vines) bore many grapes"""""
"5711","It was narrated that Ibn Sirin said:\\""Sell it as juice to one who will make At-Tila' (thickened grape juice) with it"""""
"5712","It was narrated that Suwiad bin Ghafalah said:\\""Umar bin Al-Khattab wrote to some of his workers saying: 'Give to the Muslims thickened grape juice when two thirds of it have gone and one-third is left"""""
"5713","It was narrated that 'Amir bin 'Abdullah said:\\""I saw the letter of 'Umar bin Al-Khattab to Abu Musa (in which he said): 'A caravan came to me from Ash-Sham carrying a thick black paint like the pitch that is daubed on camels. I asked them how long they cooked it"""""
"5714","It was narrated that 'Abdullah bin Yazid Al-Khatmi said:\\""Umar bin Al-Khattab"""""
"5715","It was narrated that Suwiad bin Ghafalah said:\Umar bin Al-Khattab wrote to some of his workers saying: 'Give to the Muslims thickened grape juice when two thirds of it have gone and one-third is left.'\"""""""
"5716","It was narrated that Dawud said:\\""I asked Sa'eed: 'What is the drink that 'Umar bin Al-Khattab"""""
"5717","It was narrated from Sa'eed bin Al-Musayyab that :Abu Ad-Darda' used to drink that of which two-third had gone and one-third was left"
"5718","It was narrated from Abu Musa Al-'Ash'ari that:He used to drink thickened grape juice that of which two-third had gone and one-third was left"
"5719","It was narrated that Ya'la bin 'Ata' said:\\""I heard Sa'eed bin Al-Musayyab say"""""
"5720","It was narrated that Sa'eed bin Al-Musayyab said:\\""When At-Tila' (thickened grape juice) has been cooked and reduced to one-third"""""
"5721","Abu Raja' said:\\""I asked Al-Hasan about At-Tila' (thickened grape juice) that has been reduced to half. He said: 'Do not drink it"""""
"5722","It was narrated that Bushair bin Al-Muhajir said:\\""I asked Al-Hasan about juice that has been cooked. He said: 'That which has been cooked until two-third of it has gone and one-third is left"""""
"5723","It was narrated that Anas bin Sirin said:\\""I heard Anas bin Malik say: 'The Shaitan disputed with Nuh"""""
"5724","It was narrated that 'Abdul-Malik bin Tufail Al-Jazari said:\\""Umar bin 'Abdul-'Aziz wrote to us (saying): 'Do not drink At-Tila' (thickened grape juice) until two-third of it are gone and one-third remains"""""
"5725","It was narrated that Makhul said:\\""Every intoxicant is unlawful"""""
"5726","It was narrated that Abu Thabit Ath-Tha'labi said:\\""I was with Ibn 'Abbas when a man came to him and asked him about juice. He said: 'Drink that which is fresh.' He said: 'I cooked a drink on the fire and I am not sure about it.' He said: 'Did you drink it before you cooked it?' He said: 'No.' He said: 'Fire does not make permissible something that is forbidden.'\""\"" (Sahih Mawquf)"""""
"5727","It was narrated that 'Abdul-Malik bin Tufail Al-Jazari said:\Umar bin 'Abdul-'Aziz wrote to us (saying): 'Do not drink At-Tila' (thickened grape juice) until two-third of it are gone and one-third remains"
"5728","It was narrated that Sa'eed bin Al-Musayyab said:\\""Drink juice so long as it does not have any foam"""""
"5729","It was narrated that Hisham bin 'A'idh Al-Asadi said:\\""I asked Ibrahim about juice and he said: 'Drink it"""""
"5730","'Ata' said:\I heard Ibn 'Abbas say: 'By Allah"
"5731","It was narrated that Ash-Sha'bi said:\\""Drink it for three days unless it bubbles"""""
"5732","It was narrated from 'Abdullah Ad-Dailami that his father Fairuz said:\\""I came to the Messenger of Allah [SAW] and said: 'O Messenger of Allah"""""
"5733","It was narrated from Ibn Al-Dailami that his father said:\\""We said: 'O Messenger of Allah"""""
"5734","It was narrated that Ibn 'Abbas said:\\""Nabidh would be made for the Messenger of Allah [SAW] and he would drink it in the morning"""""
"5735","It was narrated from Ibn 'Abbas that:Raisins would be soaked for the Messenger of Allah [SAW] and he would drink it that day"
"5736","It was narrated that Ibn 'Abbas said:\\""Nabidh of raisins would be made for the Messenger of Allah [SAW] at night"""""
"5737","It was narrated from Ibn 'Umar that:Nabidh of raisins would be made for him in a water skin in the morning"
"5738","It was narrated that Bassam said:\\""I asked Abu Ja'far about Nabidh and he said: \""\"" 'Ali bin Husain"""""
"5739","Abdullah said:\\""I heard Sufyan being asked about Nabidh. He said: 'Make Nabidh at night and drink it in the morning"""""
"5740","It was narrated from Ibn 'Umar that:Nabidh of raisins would be made for him in a water skin in the morning, and he would drink it that night, and it would be made for him in the evening, and he would drink it in the morning. He would wash out the water skins and not leave any pieces or anything in them. Nafi' said: \We used to drink it like honey.\"""""""
"5741","It was narrated from Sa'eed bin Al-Musayyib that:He disliked putting the dregs of Nabidh into (new) Nabidh lest it become strong because of the dregs"
"5742","It was narrated that Sa'eed bin Al-Musayyab said concerning Nabidh:\\""The dregs are what intoxicates"""""
"5743","It was narrated that Sa'eed bin Al-Musayyab said:\\""Khamr is so called because it is left until the good parts are gone and the dregs remain.\""\"" And he disliked everything that was made by using dregs (by adding new materials to the dregs)"""""
"5744","It was narrated that Ibrahim said:\\""They used to think that whoever drank something and became intoxicated from it"""""
"5745","It was narrated that Ibrahim said:\\""There is nothing wrong with Nabidh Al-Bukhtuj"""""
"5746","It was narrated that Abu Al-Miskin said:\\""I asked Ibrahim: 'We take the dregs of Khamr or Tila' (thickened grape juice) and clean them"""""
"5747","It was narrated that Ibn Shubrumah said:\\""May Allah have mercy on Ibrahim. Other scholars had strict views on Nabidh but he was lenient"""""
"5748","It was narrated that Ibrahim said:\There is nothing wrong with Nabidh Al-Bukhtuj.\"""""""
"5749","Ubaidullah bin Sa'eed said:\\""I heard Abu Usamah say: 'I never saw any man more assiduous in seeking knowledge than 'Abdullah bin Al-Mubarak"""""
"5750","It was narrated that Anas said:Umm Sulaim had a wooden cup and she said: \\""I gave the Messenger of Allah [SAW] all kinds of things to drink in it: Water"""""
"5751","It was narrated from Sa'eed bin 'Abdur-Rahman bin Abza that his father said:\\""I asked Ubayy bin Ka'b about Nabidh"""""
"5752","It was narrated that Ibn Mas'ud said:\\""The people have invented new drinks and I do not know what they are. I have not drunk anything for 20 years (or he said: 40 years) except water and Sawiq (barley gruel)"""""
"5753","It was narrated that 'Abidah said:\\""The people have invented drinks and I do not know what they are. I have not drunk anything for 20 years except water"""""
"5754","It was narrated that Ibn Shubrumah said:\\""Talhah said to the people of Al-Kufah concerning Nabidh: 'It is a test whereby a young man may benefit but an old man may be harmed.' If there was a wedding among them"""""
"5755","Jarir said:\\""Ibn Shubrumah would not drink anything except water and milk"""""
"5756","It was narrated that 'Abidah said:n The people have invented drinks and I do not know what they are. I have not drunk anything for 20 years except water, milk and honey. nSunnan e Nisai Hadees: 5759 Arabic Hadees: 5759"
"5757","It was narrated that Ibn Shubrumah said:n Talhah said to the people of Al-Kufah concerning Nabidh: 'It is a test whereby a young man may benefit but an old man may be harmed.' If there was a wedding among them, Talhah and Zubaid would offer milk and honey to drink. It was said to Talhah: 'Why don't you offer Nabidh?' He said: 'I would not like a Muslim to become intoxicated because of me.' nSunnan e Nisai Hadees: 5760 Arabic Hadees: 5760"
"5758","Jarir said:n Ibn Shubrumah would not drink anything except water and milk. nSunnan e Nisai Hadees: 5761 Arabic Hadees: 5761"
